    "statement": "For all divergence-free Fourier fields on the N^3 grid with N<=16, dealiased convective term, nu=0.1, kinetic energy = 0.5, evolved with ETD-RK2 (dt=1e-3) to T=0.02, the enstrophy E_ens(T) <= M with M=10.994055804604205. FINITE-DIMENSIONAL only. Existence of some finite max per N is trivial by compactness; explicit M is the claim.",
